Root-cause summary

Two distinct upgrade problems were resolved before the final local restart-loop issue became visible:

Release-set problem: core 2026.7.2-beta.6 existed without matching beta.6 first-party plugin packages. 
Moving to the exact complete 2026.7.2-beta.7 release set eliminated that mismatch.

Plugin-provenance problem: Brave and llama.cpp stayed on old ClawHub install records until explicitly 
replaced with pinned npm beta.7 installations.

Local watchdog problem: a custom WhatsApp timer still invoked the removed legacy OpenClaw CLI path. 
Its rc=127 was treated as a WhatsApp outage, so it restarted a healthy Gateway repeatedly. 
Correcting the CLI path, treating probe errors as unknown rather than confirmed failure, 
and reducing the timer to 15 minutes restored stable operation.

